Translation patch: keystore2::globals::get_remotely_provisioned_component_name

Change: keystore2/src/globals.rs:433, 441: each `format!` on these lines is replaced, on the same line, by a block that builds the same `String` with `to_owned`, `push_str` and `to_string`: both service names (TRUSTED_ENVIRONMENT and STRONGBOX) are built from the descriptor followed by the literal `/default` or `/strongbox`.
Why: the translation models the arguments of `format!` as `()` (`core::fmt::Arguments` is `Unit` in the Aeneas library), so the translated function gave the same service name for both security levels. `to_owned`, `push_str` and `to_string` are translated as calls whose results depend on their arguments.
Behaviour: unchanged. Each branch builds the descriptor followed by its literal suffix, as before. `Display` of a string or an integer with no format options writes the same bytes as `push_str` of the string or of the integer's `to_string`. The string is built at the same point and lives at least as long; no panic is added or removed (allocation failure aborts in both).
Classification: B
Assumptions: none.
Obligations: fork === upstream: the rewritten function behaves as the original on every input.
Evidence: an independent equivalence review by three reviewers, accepted on 2 of 3; summarised in formal/EXTRACTION-ISSUES.md.
Independent: yes

